I want to point out that this conversation has been focused on degenerate modes
only, where label switching is a consequence of non-identified latent labels.  But
once you add a measurement model and data in complex mixture models you often
get true multi modality in the posterior, where the modes are not equivalent (LDA
being a classic example of this).  In this case none of the strategies discussed are
valid and one has to adopt a more sophisticated approach.  In particular, in practice
it is critical to verify that any modes being considered are actually degenerate.

