On Wednesday, November 16, 2016 at 10:33:38 PM UTC-5, Stephen Martin wrote:
> How is it switching position with second and third? I can see how this would happen if you have three factors all loading on all items, but each factor loads on unique items.

The only constraints are that each of the 3 factors has one positive loading with the rest unrestricted. Suppose those positive loadings are 0.3, 0.5, and 0.7. You get the same posterior log-kernel if you permute the factors so that the positive loadings are 0.5, 0.7, and 0.3. Or any other permutation.

Ben

