That wasn't a problem with Stan coding so much as
figuring out what the marginalized density was.  I realize
this is hard for a lot of our users, so thanks for sharing
the example.  The usual problem is the opposite---people building
a global mixture where they want an item-by-item mixture.  You
can run into the same problem in JAGS/BUGS depending on how you
code the discrete parameter indicating the responsibility for
a mixture component.

- Bob

