If you marginalized everything but theta out for a conditional
sampler, you're left with sampling from a univariate density.  So
in this case, the bulk of the speed's going to come from marginalizing.

Then it's just going to come down to slice sampling vs. HMC or
something.  How well those compare will depend on factors of
the density being sampled.  You could probably use the zeroes (or ones?)
trick in JAGS/BUGS to implement this.  But then you're just comparing
their implementations of these algorithms.

- Bob

